        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: delete dead infra and config exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\nAI-assisted: implemented and reviewed with Codex.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe enforced production-mode Knip ratchet still carried 593 dead-export entries under `src/config` (214) and `src/infra` (379). Those exports unnecessarily enlarged internal module surfaces and kept tests coupled to code that production never imports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis removes export modifiers where implementations remain useful internally, deletes code and tests that existed only for dead exports, and keeps production/config contracts that are consumed by runtime callers, schema generation, or documented surfaces. Tests retained for meaningful behavior now exercise production APIs instead of re-exported test helpers. The dead-export baseline was regenerated on the exact tested head immediately before push; subsequent `main` drift did not touch the baseline, `src/config`, or `src/infra`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended runtime or config behavior change. The internal TypeScript surface is smaller, dead test-only code is gone, and the enforced baseline drops every `src/config` and `src/infra` entry so future regressions are blocked by CI.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head Testbox `tbx_01kxd5mz084bc6teqsgq1kbas6` on `54a6ecd0f803ae2ddc336e5b55f4a5519077a733`: `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` generated 4,267 entries, then `pnpm deadcode:exports` passed.\n- The same run passed `pnpm tsgo:prod`, `pnpm tsgo:scripts`, `pnpm tsgo:test`, `pnpm check:architecture`, `pnpm build`, and 472 focused tests across infra, gateway run-loop, ACP command dispatch, and auto-reply.\n- Baseline SHA-256: `1ebdec54303cae8e0c47d1ecbd1a4c0788445b8ef5406f9ae3d010d72d84ce12`; zero entries begin with `src/config/` or `src/infra/`.\n- Session-accessor debt SHA-256: `6cdd7ab44a53b1e4699945345c7435dacbe013f42e99f837257f074fe3ca9e79`; its boundary guard passed on the exact head.\n- Autoreview: coherent implementation slices and the final integration/repair diffs completed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: clean.\n",
